cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Crystallization Contest: reward schemes between agents and a 3-membrane contest (SYNTHETIC)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-24"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/crystallization-contest"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC classical simulation, standard-library Python. Compares five
  reward schemes between agents (individual, team, difference, consensus,
  random) on a harness-defined crystallization event at widths 32 to 512,
  with every event labelled true or false against the generator's ground
  truth, and runs a contest of three coupled membranes with a shield, an
  amplifier and a stabilizer, including a stabilizer stress test and a
  false-event-cost variant. Reports negative results: the amplifier has no
  measurable effect, the stabilizer lowers variance at a cost in precision,
  and charging false events did not raise precision.
keywords:
  - "reward-schemes"
  - "multi-agent"
  - "streaming-pca"
  - "synthetic"
  - "classical-simulation"
  - "python"
